From: Andrei Vagin <avagin@google.com>
Subject: [PATCH] restore: preserve the complete eight-bit zombie exit status

Backport of castai/criu e956db75f7a60c883daf9440a3ffed909515d2f1
("restore: Fix exit code truncation for zombies").
The wait-status exit field has eight bits. Retain the high bit when the
restored zombie exits. Signal handling and every upstream assertion remain
unchanged. This modification retains the CRIU source file's GPL-2.0 terms.

Signed-off-by: Andrei Vagin <avagin@google.com>
--- a/criu/cr-restore.c
+++ b/criu/cr-restore.c
@@ -975,7 +975,7 @@ static int restore_one_zombie(CoreEntry *core)
 		exit_code = 0;
 	}
 
-	exit((exit_code >> 8) & 0x7f);
+	exit((exit_code >> 8) & 0xff);
 
 	/* never reached */
 	BUG_ON(1);
